From 886431218ed77928629fc6e53c7e5de0e955db5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Conrado <30303391+CPontes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:15:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] msgq: 25 reader slots, as openpilot's msgq since commaai/msgq
 d44b74a

gomsgq v0.1.12 takes the reader slots per queue; mapd passes MSGQ_MAX_READERS (25), or the MSGQ_MAX_READERS environment
variable for an older msgq (15). With 15 on our side and 25 on openpilot's the queue header is 240 bytes off: openpilot never
reads mapdOut, and mapd reads its inputs from the wrong place (LizPilot MAP-01/MAP-02).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
